      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-04-10_WidnesExaminer_art0024" n="art0024">
        <head>Major Appleton.</head>
        <p>Major Appleton.</p>
        <p>The" London Gazette" of Tuesday evening e:„ tamed the following announcement :—" 4th Battali°; The Prince of Wales' Volunteers (South LancashiL" Itegiment).—Captain and Hon. Major (lion. cart' in the Army) F. M. Appleton to be major; datedill it January, 1909."—Major Appleton's connection w the Territorials has been a long and honcurable °Ile; He was appointed second-lieutenant on Decetebe`f 21st, 1887, when he - was posted to &amp;Compaq ° which Colonel Buckton was then • captain; vrhile the 14th September, 1889, he Was made lieutenant"( On March sth, 1893, he was promoted to the rank ° captain, being in command of C Compinv Until 115 left for South Africa where he served in charge el Warrington's first Volunteer active service comPao for about eighteen mouths. For some time while .1t Warrington Mayor Appleton directed the CyC section of the corps, and he successfully rassed tactics. It may be remembered that Major AFernlet°' was selected to command a detachment of 20 mete who were on guard in London on the occasion of t°o late Queen's Diamond Jubilee celebration. The In:31, were stationed on Westminster Bridge, and the waJ° had the honour of receiving a jubilee medal.</p>
      </div>
