      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-04-10_WidnesExaminer_art0027" n="art0027">
        <p>,</p>
        <p>ti L</p>
        <p>Ilowl e iat;rington are still progressing steadily towards e'e• That is, they are moving up the League 14_,..inhout any hope of reaching the top. Already 1314%,, oe left the halfway house—their usual resting ,1111;5;---e2ns1derably in the rear, and have passed such Runslet and Hull in the race. It is rather Al' to uote bow high some of the lowly stand— lilyerthYr ! With their Welsh League fixtures, and tait,"„sual engagements outside their native moun- "leY have built up a record which has taken .I'her 4ithia measurable distance of the •first four. ,ave been anomalies in the League before, but e,,,,i111Yr and Ebbw Vale were to reach the top By p„ille,aus in same future season there would be fOr a—nai.tiVe demands from Lancashire and Yorks:hire. '4ange.</p>
